  <data name="Act_RestructBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This version of OMniX has a new folder structure.

Characters are now organized by category, with one folder per category, in this layout:
Mods/Category/Character/&lt;Mod folder&gt;
So until things are reorganized, OMniX won't see your existing mods.
This is a one-time thing, and you can also reorganize them yourself.

Character folders are now created on demand, and you can also clean up empty folders in the settings page.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Act_RestructHelpMe" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reorganize for me</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Act_RestructMyself" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>I'll do it myself</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Act_RestructNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>
This dialog will keep showing until you choose one of the options below. There is also a "Reorganize" button in the settings page.
Check the log if you want to see what exactly happened.</value>
  </data>
